  "supportFallback": "I can't answer right now. Try again in a little while, and if it keeps happening, open the “Crash log” on this screen and send it to us — it has what we need to fix it.",
  "supportFaqBank": "To let Zad read your bank messages: on Home, tap “Turn on bank notification reading” and follow the steps. If the switch is grey or you see “Restricted setting”: open “App info” → ⋮ at the top → “Allow restricted settings”, then come back and turn the permission on. On Xiaomi and Oppo, set the battery to “No restrictions” so it doesn't stop.",
  "supportFaqAllowance": "In “Family” → “Kids' spending” you'll find each child and their balance. “Send allowance” adds to it straight away. A child can ask for an “allowance” (added if you approve) or to “buy something” (deducted if you approve and the balance covers it).",
  "supportFaqReceipt": "Snap the receipt with the camera button. Zad reads the total, the items and the receipt's date, and logs it on that day. Check the amount and the category before saving — you can add the items to the pantry in the same step.",
  "supportFaqCountry": "Your country and currency are set when you sign up. To change them: “My account” → “Region”. Times and reminders follow the account's country.",
  "supportFaqVoice": "Tap the mic in the chat and talk — Zad answers out loud. If the answer is slow or there's no sound, check your internet and try again; the written reply stays in the chat.",
  "supportFaqAppointments": "Add appointments from “My appointments” → “New appointment”, or tell Zad in the chat “remind me of the doctor on Thursday at 5”. Medicines live in “Family pharmacy”, where you can say who in the family each one is for.",
  "supportFaqFamily": "In “Family”, start a new family and send the code to your people, or tap “Join” and enter the code you got. Only the admin can change roles and rewards.",
  "supportFaqPassword": "On the sign-in screen, tap “Forgot password” and enter your email — you'll get a link to change it.",
  "supportFaqDeleteAccount": "Delete your account from “My account” → “Delete account”. It erases all your data for good, with no way back.",
  "supportWelcome": "Hi! I'm Zad's help assistant — I can explain any feature or sort out a technical problem. If your question is about your own data (spending, balance, subscriptions), ask the \"Zad's brain\" chat instead: it's the only one that sees your actual account.",
