  "supportTermsHeading": "Terms of Use and User Agreement",
  "supportTermsIntro": "Last updated: July 2026\n\nPlease read these terms of use carefully before using Zad.",
  "supportTerms1Title": "1. Accepting the terms",
  "supportTerms1Body": "By creating an account or using Zad, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the app.",
  "supportTerms2Title": "2. What the service is — a tool, not a responsible party",
  "supportTerms2Body": "Zad is an organising and personal-assistance tool only. We provide software that helps you track, organise and view your own financial and household data. We do not manage your money, make decisions on your behalf, hold your funds, process payments, or act as a financial institution, financial adviser or fiduciary of any kind.\n\nEvery feature in the app — including budgeting, expense tracking, receipt scanning, pantry tracking, subscription tracking, transaction detection from notifications, and any \"smart\" or \"AI-based\" insight — exists only to help you organise information you already have or produce. We do not verify, guarantee or take responsibility for the accuracy of that information, or for any action you take based on it.\n\nYou, and only you, are responsible for:\n- every financial decision you make;\n- checking the accuracy of any data the app shows, calculates, detects or suggests;\n- the results of relying on any automated feature, including AI-generated insights or forecasts and detection from notifications;\n- every outcome relating to your budget, spending, savings or household management, whether or not the app's information is accurate.\n\nWe accept no responsibility or liability of any kind for the results of your use of the app. Using Zad does not create any advisory relationship, fiduciary duty or guarantee of any outcome between you and us. The app is offered purely as an organising and convenience tool — how you use the information it shows is entirely your responsibility.",
  "supportTerms3Title": "3. Privacy and data",
  "supportTerms3Body": "We respect your privacy. Your data is stored securely. We do not sell your personal financial data to any third party.",
  "supportTerms4Title": "4. Third-party AI features — assistance only, not authoritative",
  "supportTerms4Body": "Some features (receipt scanning, spending forecasts, subscription detection, behavioural insights, meal suggestions, voice input) use third-party AI services to process data and generate suggestions. These outputs are offered as a convenience only and must never be treated as accurate, complete, verified or authoritative. AI-generated content may be wrong, out of date or unsuitable for your situation.\n\nWe do not own or control the AI models used. We are not responsible for anything the AI generates, suggests, predicts or fails to detect. You must check any number, category or recommendation yourself before acting on it. Relying on any AI output as financial guidance is entirely at your own risk.",
  "supportTerms5Title": "5. Family sharing",
  "supportTerms5Body": "If you invite family members, you are responsible for their access to your household's data.",
  "supportTerms6Title": "6. Prohibited conduct",
  "supportTerms6Body": "You may not reverse-engineer or hack Zad, or use it for any unlawful activity.",
  "supportTerms7Title": "7. We provide the tool — you are responsible for the outcome",
  "supportTerms7Body": "We do not guarantee, and take no responsibility for, the accuracy of any balance, expense category, subscription status, stock level, low-stock alert or budget forecast shown in the app. Nor do we guarantee that automatic transaction detection will catch every transaction, or that it will always be right when it does.\n\nBy using Zad, you acknowledge that:\n- we are a passive information-organising tool, not an active party to your financial decisions;\n- any financial loss, missed payment, overspending, spoiled stock, family disagreement or other negative outcome arising from your use of or reliance on the app is your responsibility alone;\n- we will accept no liability, financial or otherwise, for those outcomes, to the fullest extent permitted by law.",
